  "conclusions": [
    "Final 640-frame integrated runtime reported zero failures after correcting walking checks to observe the configured 0.45-second lower duration. The alpha<.01 threshold was unchanged.",
    "Steady combat guard wrists/fingers have zero local rotation changes and feet have zero component position steps; the tiny remaining motion comes from the authored thoracic breath and retargeted head compensation.",
    "The overall 53cm/110degree finger component-space step occurs in the early Knuckle Jab montage blend. The baseline already had a 54cm/110degree step at identical montage time; the new stance changes only the early blend, with a slightly faster initial raise and then identical full montage pose samples.",
    "Root helper world height differs between imported boxing and standard idle representations; the pelvis compensates that offset. Actual foot world height differences remain below3cm and source/appearance component and capsule transformations reported zero displacement. Root helper height is diagnostic, not a floating-body failure.",
    "These results do not claim that all combat transitions are jitter free. They confirm stable sustained combat stance and existing bounded head-camera behavior while isolating inherited early attack/montage blend motion."
  ],
